      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**. \n\nSpecifically, it explains that before overwriting any file, the guarded tool executor records that file\u0027s prior state\u2014either its previous content (if it existed) or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist\u2014into an in-memory write journal. If the agent run fails (due to a turn cap being exceeded, an unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll every recorded write back in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed, and deleting newly created files. This approach provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction\u2014the journal itself serves as the transaction log, kept only in the process\u0027s memory for the duration of one run.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses this journal\u0027s rollback path because it has no write tool at all.",
